    "# Day 1 – Introduction to Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. What is Machine Learning?\n",
    "\n",
    "Machine Learning (ML) is a branch of Artificial Intelligence (AI) that enables computers to learn patterns from data and make predictions or decisions without being explicitly programmed for every task.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example\n",
    "\n",
    "A machine learning model can learn from previous house prices and predict the price of a new house based on features such as:\n",
    "\n",
    "- House size\n",
    "- Number of bedrooms\n",
    "- Location\n",
    "- Age of the house#%% md\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. AI vs Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "### Artificial Intelligence (AI)\n",
    "\n",
    "Artificial Intelligence is the broader field of creating machines or computer systems that can perform tasks that normally require human intelligence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Problem solving\n",
    "- Decision making\n",
    "- Speech recognition\n",
    "- Image recognition\n",
    "- Natural language understanding\n",
    "\n",
    "### Machine Learning (ML)\n",
    "\n",
    "Machine Learning is a subset of AI in which computers learn patterns from data and use those patterns to make predictions or decisions.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Relationship\n",
    "\n",
    "AI → Machine Learning → Deep Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Difference Between AI and ML\n",
    "\n",
    "| Artificial Intelligence | Machine Learning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| AI is a broad field. | ML is a subset of AI. |\n",
    "| Focuses on creating intelligent systems. | Focuses on learning from data. |\n",
    "| Can use rules, logic, ML, etc. | Uses algorithms to learn patterns from data. |\n",
    "| Example: Self-driving car system | Example: Pedestrian detection model |\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Types of Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "There are three major types of Machine Learning:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Supervised Learning\n",
    "2. Unsupervised Learning\n",
    "3. Reinforcement Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4.1 Supervised Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Supervised Learning is a type of machine learning where the model learns from **labeled data**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The input and the expected output are already known during training.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example\n",
    "\n",
    "House size, number of bedrooms and location → House price\n",
    "\n",
    "### Common Algorithms\n",
    "\n",
    "- Linear Regression\n",
    "- Logistic Regression\n",
    "- Decision Tree\n",
    "- Random Forest\n",
    "- K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)\n",
    "- Support Vector Machine (SVM)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Applications\n",
    "\n",
    "- House price prediction\n",
    "- Spam detection\n",
    "- Disease prediction\n",
    "- Student performance prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4.2 Unsupervised Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Unsupervised Learning is a type of machine learning where the model works with **unlabeled data**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The model tries to discover hidden patterns or groups within the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example\n",
    "\n",
    "Customer data → Groups customers with similar behavior\n",
    "\n",
    "### Common Algorithms\n",
    "\n",
    "- K-Means Clustering\n",
    "- Hierarchical Clustering\n",
    "- Principal Component Analysis (PCA)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Applications\n",
    "\n",
    "- Customer segmentation\n",
    "- Market analysis\n",
    "- Anomaly detection\n",
    "- Pattern recognition\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4.3 Reinforcement Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Reinforcement Learning is a type of machine learning where an **agent learns by interacting with an environment**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The agent performs actions and receives rewards or penalties.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Basic Process\n",
    "\n",
    "Agent → Action → Environment → Reward/Penalty → Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "### Applications\n",
    "\n",
    "- Game-playing AI\n",
    "- Robotics\n",
    "- Autonomous vehicles\n",
    "- Industrial automation\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Real-World Applications of Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Machine Learning is used in many real-world applications.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Area | Application |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Healthcare | Disease prediction and medical image analysis |\n",
    "| Banking | Fraud detection and risk analysis |\n",
    "| E-commerce | Product recommendations |\n",
    "| Entertainment | Movie and music recommendations |\n",
    "| Email | Spam detection |\n",
    "| Transportation | Self-driving vehicles |\n",
    "| Security | Face recognition |\n",
    "| Chatbots | Natural Language Processing |\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6. Machine Learning Workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "A typical Machine Learning workflow consists of the following steps:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Problem Definition\n",
    "2. Data Collection\n",
    "3. Data Cleaning\n",
    "4. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "5. Feature Engineering\n",
    "6. Train-Test Split\n",
    "7. Model Selection\n",
    "8. Model Training\n",
    "9. Model Evaluation\n",
    "10. Prediction\n",
    "11. Deployment\n",
    "12. Monitoring and Improvement\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. ML Workflow Diagram\n",
    "\n",
    "Problem Definition\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Data Collection\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Data Cleaning\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Feature Engineering\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Train-Test Split\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Model Selection\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Model Training\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Model Evaluation\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Prediction\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Deployment\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "Monitoring & Improvement\n",
    "\n",
    "## 8. Example: House Price Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we want to predict the price of a house.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Input Features\n",
    "\n",
    "- House size\n",
    "- Number of bedrooms\n",
    "- Location\n",
    "- Age of house\n",
    "\n",
    "### Workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "House Data\n",
    "↓\n",
    "Clean Data\n",
    "↓\n",
    "Analyze Data\n",
    "↓\n",
    "Select Features\n",
    "↓\n",
    "Split Data\n",
    "↓\n",
    "Train ML Model\n",
    "↓\n",
    "Evaluate Model\n",
    "↓\n",
    "Predict House Price\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an example of **Supervised Learning** because the training data contains the actual house prices as labels."
